resources.string:
To run Linux in a virtual machine, AndLin needs a companion app, %1$s.

If you continue, AndLin will:

• download %1$s (%2$s) from AndLin's GitHub releases;
• ask you to turn on Wireless debugging in Developer options and pair AndLin with your own device, so it can act like a computer connected over ADB;
• install %1$s and grant it the permissions it needs: running virtual machines, all files access (only used when you choose to share your device's storage with a session), and notifications.

Nothing leaves your device other than the download. You can turn Wireless debugging off again when this is done, and uninstall %1$s any time.
